wikipedia_extract: I-36 was an Imperial Japanese Navy B1 type submarine. Completed
  and commissioned in 1942, she served in World War II, operating in the Guadalcanal
  campaign, New Guinea campaign, Aleutian Islands campaign, and the Marshall Islands.
  She finished the war as a kaiten manned suicide attack torpedo carrier, operating
  against Allied ships at Ulithi Atoll and in the Philippine Sea. The only submarine
  of her class to survive the war, she surrendered to the Allies in September 1945
  after the end of the war and was scuttled by the United States Navy in 1946.
